<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2492" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ancillŭla</span></b> , ae, f.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>doub. dim.</i>
			[id.], <i>a little serving-maid</i>, <i>a
				young female slave.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Plaut.
				Rud. prol. 74</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ter. Heaut. 2, 3, 11</span></i>; so <i><span class="en">id. Eun. 1,
				2, 86</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Phorm. 5, 5, 10 al.</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nec servus nec ancillula, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. R. Am. 639 al.</span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">juris scientiam eloquentiae tamquam ancillulam
					pedissequamque adjunxisti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de
					Or. 1, 55 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praesto esse virtutes ut ancillulas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Fin. 2, 21, 69</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
